# SPA fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Routing happens in the browser, so only `/` exists as a real file. Without
# this, refreshing on /dashboard/logs — or opening a shared link to it — asks
# the host for a file that was never built and gets a 404 before the router
# ever runs. Serve index.html for everything and let the router resolve it.
#
# 200, not 302: the URL must survive so the router can read it.
/*    /index.html   200
